<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="sec-14-writing-assignments-long">
  <title>Writing Assignments</title>

  <p>
    Writing in this course supports mathematical reasoning, communication, and reflection.
    Short writing tasks help you identify what you understand, where you are stuck, and what
    to do next.
  </p>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Check-Ins</title>
    <p>
      During a long semester, you will complete periodic check-ins to report progress,
      questions, and challenges. Check-ins may be brief, but thoughtful responses are encouraged.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Discussions</title>
    <p>
      Discussion activities support collaboration and help you practice explaining ideas clearly.
      Follow netiquette and course expectations for respectful participation.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>AI Policy for Writing</title>
    <p>
      Unless assignment instructions explicitly permit otherwise, submit your own original thinking.
      You may use generative AI for editing clarity and organization only when course policy allows
      and with proper citation.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
</subsection>
